{%- comment -%}
  Free Spirited — coupon rules for Insider-side verification.

  Emits the rules the theme can verify itself (minimum-purchase, type, value)
  so fs-discount.js can check a code against the INSIDER subtotal and decide
  whether to display its discount. This is what lets minimum-purchase codes
  work in Insider mode without a live API call.

  Place this INSIDE the drawer markup wrapped by [data-cart-drawer] (near the
  [data-fs-discount-data] script) so it re-renders with the ajax-cart section.

  DATA SOURCE (demo): a shop-level JSON metafield you fill in by hand.
    Admin → Settings → Custom data → Shop → metafield `custom.coupon_rules`
    Type: JSON. Example value:
      [
        { "code": "10OFFVIP",   "min": 2500, "type": "fixed",   "value": 1000 },
        { "code": "CREDIT1195", "min": 3500, "type": "fixed",   "value": 1195 },
        { "code": "SUMMER10",   "min": 0,    "type": "percent", "value": 10 }
      ]
  Units: min and (fixed) value in CENTS; percent value is a number (10 = 10%).

  Codes WITHOUT an entry here are treated as unverifiable for anything beyond a
  plain unconditional percentage — fs-discount.js hides them in Insider mode.

  For production, swap this JSON metafield for a metaobject (one entry per code)
  if the client needs a friendlier admin UI; the JS reads the same shape.
{%- endcomment -%}

<script type="application/json" data-fs-coupon-rules>
  {{ shop.metafields.custom.coupon_rules.value | default: '[]' | json }}
</script>
